# Warps 4 to 7 run <block 2> where the byte each reads at
# ⌊%tid.x/32⌋ + state is 0. A load at an address a warp's lanes read
# alike gives them one value, so the block runs under a warp-uniform
# condition, on all lanes of a warp or on none, of warps 4 to 7: at
# most 128 threads, but the store's sectors per warp request are a
# range, not a bound.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/warp_dispatch.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	mul.wide.u32 	%rd3, %r1, 4; // [<block 2>] warp 4-7 × lane * | runs when %rs1@35 = 0 (warp-uniform, branch at line 37) | exec <= 128/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store [4·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req 4–5 (ideal 4){{$}}
